notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T06:09:40.075Z","harness:codex","Verification observation 2026-09-08: a full heavily parallel coverage run completed 8559 passing tests but the standalone context-read-cost default workload hit the existing 3000ms usage-ledger lock wait at four writers. The same two-test benchmark suite passed alone in 6.02 seconds, with its real concurrent writer/byte/recall assertions intact. Do not infer a source regression or a fleet-scale pass from either result. Preserve contention/latency receipts and repeat the full suite with bounded worker concurrency after tracker mutation work settles. The production lock bound was not increased and the failure was not hidden by weakening an assertion."
